/-!
# The memLevel 2 overlay certificate (`lit_bufsize = 256`)

Generated by `tests/goals/overlay-adversarial/certificate/overlay_cert.py --lean`; do not edit.
The test `certificate/regenerate.sh` regenerates it and compares.

For the literal/length tree (lengths `ll`, actual frequencies `fl`, 286 entries) and the
distance tree (`dl`, `fd`, 30 entries) of one block with at most 255 symbols:

  `71 + Σ entryCost (ll v) + Σ entryCost (dl v) + E ≤ 1852`,

`E` the excess per occurrence: `x + e − 9` for a length code, `x + e − 15` for a distance code.
Facts used: Kraft per tree, the Fibonacci bound `f·F(x+1) + F(x) ≤ 258` for used codes, unused
codes with a nonzero length only at index ≤ 2, the end-of-block frequency 1, at most 255
symbols, as many length codes as distance codes. The certificate is a set of multipliers,
scaled by 262144: each entry costs at most its share (`entry_*`, a sixteen-case `omega` check),
and the shares add up to the bound.
-/

